// Requires astroCmsPipeline (planned, see esoul-infrastructure docs/plan)
//
// The only Jenkinsfile of the monorepo (multibranch job with the default scriptPath). `astroCmsPipeline` does not
// exist yet; this is the configuration it is meant to take. Replace the example values with the project's own.
//
// What the step is meant to do (frontend/ = Astro static site, backend/ = Laravel + Filament CMS):
//  - Plan: decide from the changed paths what runs. Pull requests and other branches: backend tests when
//    backend/ changed, frontend checks when frontend/ or backend/tests/Fixtures/ changed. main: backend tests +
//    image + Komodo deploy when backend/ changed, website build + static deploy when frontend/ changed, on a
//    manual start, or on a publish from the admin. A publish (parameter CMS_PUBLISH_ID) builds and deploys only the
//    website and reports back.
//  - Backend (docker/production/Dockerfile): composer install, pint, phpstan, php artisan test, composer audit;
//    on main build + push the multi-arch image and deploy the Komodo stack. Same stages as laravelPipeline.
//  - Frontend checks (no backend needed): pnpm install --frozen-lockfile, then the default Astro check set:
//    pnpm audit, pnpm lint (ESLint), pnpm format:check, pnpm fixture:check, pnpm check (astro check; plus
//    vue-tsc --noEmit when the site has Vue islands), pnpm build, pnpm verify, pnpm test:e2e (Playwright smoke,
//    desktop + mobile). check, build, verify and test:e2e run with an explicit CMS_SOURCE=fixture.
//  - Website build (main / publish): backend is deployed first, then pnpm install --frozen-lockfile, check, build,
//    verify with CMS_SOURCE=api, CMS_API_URL, CMS_API_TOKEN (credential) and SITE_URL. The fixture is never allowed
//    here: the build fails when the export is unreachable. CONTENT_HASH is read from node_modules/.astro/cms/source.json.
//  - Static deploy on an agent labelled `deploy`, under a lock: deployStaticSite(sourceDir: 'dist/',
//    deployPath, sharedDirs: ['_astro']) -> <deployPath>/current -> releases/<id> (docker/nginx.example).
//  - post { always }: when CMS_PUBLISH_ID is set, POST {cmsApiUrl}/publishes/<id>/status with
//    `Authorization: Bearer <callback token>` and {result, buildUrl, contentHash}. A failing callback never fails
//    the build; the admin falls back to polling Jenkins (Publish page, "Refresh status").
//  - disableConcurrentBuilds(): two publishes would overwrite each other's release.
//
// Jenkins parameter (declared by the step): CMS_PUBLISH_ID (string, empty by default, filled by the admin).
// Credentials: scaleway_secret_key, komodo_deploy_api_key, komodo_deploy_api_secret, deploy_ssh (as in
// laravelPipeline) plus the two Secret Text credentials below. The export token is CMS_EXPORT_TOKEN of
// backend/.env, the callback token is CMS_JENKINS_CALLBACK_TOKEN.
//
// The build agent fetches /cms-api over the public URL, so its address has to be in CMS_API_ALLOWED_IPS of the
// backend (README, "Publish flow").
@Library(['dockerHelpers', 'testing', 'deploy', 'pipelines']) _

astroCmsPipeline(
    // Backend: image built from backend/docker/production/Dockerfile and the Komodo stack that runs it.
    backendImage: 'example-project-be',
    backendStack: 'example-project',

    // Frontend: Node image of the checks and of the production build, pinned by version and digest.
    nodeImage: 'node:24',

    // Static site: release root on the server (current/, releases/, shared/) and the public origin.
    deployPath: '/data/apps/example-project/web',
    sharedDirs: ['_astro'],
    siteUrl: 'https://example-project.example.com',

    // Publish flow: where the build fetches the export and which credentials it uses.
    cmsApiUrl: 'https://example-project.example.com/cms-api/v1',
    exportTokenCredentialsId: 'example-project-cms-export-token',
    callbackTokenCredentialsId: 'example-project-cms-callback-token',
    publishParameter: 'CMS_PUBLISH_ID',

    deployBranches: ['main'],
)
